meta {
  name: Decide - ServiceRequest search
  type: http
  seq: 4
}

post {
  url: {{opaUrl}}/v1/data/umzh/authz/gateway/allow
  body: json
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
}

body:json {
  {
    "input": {
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "path": "/fhir/ServiceRequest",
        "query": {
          "_id": "sr-e2e"
        },
        "headers": {
          "authorization": "Bearer {{bearerToken}}"
        }
      }
    }
  }
}

docs {
  May this caller search ServiceRequest?_id=sr-e2e? OPA derives the target id from
  query._id, then applies the fhirContext + Consent graph rule (system/
  ServiceRequest.r + an active Consent naming the caller for the sr-e2e context).
  DATA-DEPENDENT (OPA fetches Consent/ServiceRequest). Response: { "result": true|false }.
}
